# Saturn Engine — Licence

**Version 0.1.0 (beta) · 11 September 2026**

> This licence is written to be read. It is not legal advice and it has not been
> reviewed by a lawyer. Before Saturn Engine leaves beta, have one read it.

Saturn Engine is two things under one download, and they are licensed
differently on purpose.

| | What it is | What you may do |
|---|---|---|
| **The Editor** | The Saturn Engine application you install and run | Use it, free, while it is in beta. Do not redistribute or reverse engineer it. |
| **The Runtime SDK** | Saturn's own GDScript that gets copied *into* the games you export (`sdk/*.gd`) | Copy, modify and ship it inside your games, forever, for free. |
| **Your Game** | Everything you make | Yours. Entirely. |

---

## 1. Definitions

**"Saturn"** means Saturn Engine and its licensor.

**"The Editor"** means the Saturn Engine desktop application, its installer, and
every file it installs, except the Runtime SDK and the third-party components
listed in section 6.

**"The Runtime SDK"** means the GDScript source files Saturn copies into a game
you export — the files under `sdk/` in the exported project, and any Saturn code
generated into your project's own source.

**"Your Game"** means any software you create using the Editor, including its
code, assets, and the binaries you export.

---

## 2. Your Game is yours

You own Your Game outright. Saturn claims no ownership of it, no copyright in
it, and no share of what it earns.

You may sell Your Game, give it away, put it on any store, keep it closed, open
its source, or abandon it. You need no permission and you owe no royalty, no
revenue share, and no reporting.

**This is permanent and it is not conditional on anything.** It survives this
licence being superseded, the Editor's terms changing, the beta ending, and
Saturn ceasing to exist. A game you ship today stays shipped on these terms
forever. Saturn cannot revoke this grant, for any version, retroactively or
otherwise.

## 3. The Runtime SDK — the part that travels with Your Game

Every game exported from Saturn carries Saturn's own GDScript inside it. Without
a licence to redistribute that code, you could not legally ship what you make,
which would make section 2 worthless.

So: Saturn grants you a **perpetual, worldwide, irrevocable, royalty-free,
sublicensable** licence to use, copy, modify and distribute the Runtime SDK as
part of Your Game, in source or compiled form.

You do not need to credit Saturn. You may not distribute the Runtime SDK on its
own, separately from a game, as a competing SDK or engine.

Like section 2, this grant is irrevocable for every copy already distributed.

## 4. The Editor

While Saturn Engine is in beta, the Editor is licensed to you free of charge,
for any purpose including commercial work, on any number of machines you
personally use.

You may not:

- redistribute, resell, rent or sublicense the Editor itself;
- reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble it, except where law expressly
  permits that despite this term;
- remove or alter its notices.

**The Editor's terms may change after beta.** A future version may cost money or
carry different conditions. That affects future versions of the Editor only.
It never reaches back to section 2 or section 3, and it never affects a game you
have already made or shipped.

## 5. Beta, warranty, and liability

Saturn Engine is beta software provided **"as is", without warranty of any
kind**, express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular
purpose, and non-infringement.

It is not code-signed, so Windows SmartScreen will warn you about an unknown
publisher. That warning is accurate: there is no certificate yet.

To the maximum extent the law allows, Saturn is not liable for any damages
arising from the software or its use — including lost work, lost data, lost
profits, or business interruption — even if told such damages were possible.

**Back up your projects.** This is beta software and you should treat it that
way.

Nothing here limits liability that cannot legally be limited, and nothing here
takes away consumer rights you have by law where you live.

## 6. Other people's work, shipped inside this

Saturn Engine distributes components owned by others, under their own licences,
which govern those components and not this one:

- **Godot Engine** — MIT licence. Copyright (c) 2014-present Godot Engine
  contributors; copyright (c) 2007-2014 Juan Linietsky, Ariel Manzur. The full
  text and the third-party notices ship with the application, under
  `resources/godot/licenses/`. Saturn Engine is not affiliated with or endorsed
  by the Godot Foundation.
- **Sample city data** — © OpenStreetMap contributors, licensed
  [ODbL 1.0](https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/). Elevation data from
  USGS 3DEP. **If you ship a game built on the bundled Salt Lake City sample,
  ODbL requires you to credit OpenStreetMap somewhere a player can find it.**
  Saturn adds that credit to exported games automatically; do not remove it.
- **Fonts** — Archivo and Geist, under the SIL Open Font License; the licence
  files ship alongside them.

## 7. Ending

This licence ends if you breach it. Sections 2 and 3 survive that, and survive
everything else: whatever happens to this agreement, Your Game stays yours and
stays shippable.

## 8. Questions, and reporting a problem

Open an issue: https://github.com/anar0226/saturn-engine-releases/issues

For a security vulnerability, see [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md) — please do not
open a public issue for one.

